{"id":"mahabharata-5-072","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":72,"title":"द्विसप्ततितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 72 · Bhima speaks for peace","summary":{"en":"To everyone's surprise Bhima urges Krishna to speak gently to Duryodhana and seek peace by every means, so that the Bharata race is not destroyed. He says that even he would bow to Duryodhana for peace, and that Arjuna too is no lover of war.","kn":"ಎಲ್ಲರಿಗೂ ಆಶ್ಚರ್ಯವಾಗುವಂತೆ, ಭರತವಂಶ ನಾಶವಾಗದಂತೆ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನೊಂದಿಗೆ ಮೃದುವಾಗಿ ಮಾತನಾಡಿ ಎಲ್ಲ ಮಾರ್ಗಗಳಿಂದ ಶಾಂತಿ ಪಡೆಯೆಂದು ಭೀಮನು ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನನ್ನು ಒತ್ತಾಯಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಶಾಂತಿಗಾಗಿ ತಾನೂ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನಿಗೆ ತಲೆಬಾಗುವೆ, ಅರ್ಜುನನೂ ಯುದ್ಧಪ್ರಿಯನಲ್ಲ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"सबको चकित करते हुए भीम श्रीकृष्ण से आग्रह करते हैं कि दुर्योधन से कोमलता से बात करें और हर उपाय से शान्ति प्राप्त करें, ताकि भरतवंश नष्ट न हो। वे कहते हैं कि शान्ति के लिए वे भी दुर्योधन के आगे झुक जाएँगे, और अर्जुन भी युद्धप्रिय नहीं हैं।","te":"అందరూ ఆశ్చర్యపోయేలా, భరతవంశం నాశనం కాకుండా దుర్యోధనునితో మృదువుగా మాట్లాడి అన్ని మార్గాల్లో శాంతి సాధించమని భీముడు శ్రీకృష్ణుని కోరతాడు. శాంతి కోసం తానూ దుర్యోధనునికి తలవంచుతానని, అర్జునుడు కూడా యుద్ధప్రియుడు కాదని అంటాడు.","ta":"அனைவரும் வியக்கும்படி, பரத குலம் அழியாதபடி துரியோதனனிடம் மென்மையாகப் பேசி எல்லா வழிகளிலும் அமைதியைப் பெறுமாறு பீமன் ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணரை வற்புறுத்துகிறான். அமைதிக்காகத் தானும் துரியோதனனுக்குத் தலைவணங்குவேன், அர்ஜுனனும் போர் விரும்பி அல்ல என்கிறான்.","ml":"എല്ലാവരെയും അത്ഭുതപ്പെടുത്തി, ദുര്യോധനനോട് മൃദുവായി സംസാരിച്ച്, ഭരതകുലം നശിക്കാതിരിക്കാൻ എല്ലാ വഴിയിലൂടെയും സമാധാനം തേടണമെന്ന് ഭീമൻ കൃഷ്ണനോട് ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു. സമാധാനത്തിനുവേണ്ടി താൻ പോലും ദുര്യോധനന് മുന്നിൽ തലകുനിക്കുമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു; അർജുനനും യുദ്ധപ്രിയനല്ലെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.72; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"भगवद्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Bhagavadyana Parva (Krishna's embassy)","verses":[{"text":"भीमसेन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"यथा यथैव शान्तिः स्यात्कुरूणां मधुसूदन ।\nतथा तथैव भाषेथा मा स्म युद्धेन भीषयेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhusudana, speak in whatever way will bring peace among the Kurus; do not frighten them with talk of war."}},{"n":2,"text":"अमर्षी नित्यसंरब्धः श्रेयोद्वेषी महामनाः ।\nनोग्रं दुर्योधनो वाच्यः साम्नैवैनं समाचरेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana is intolerant, always agitated, hostile to his own good and proud; do not speak harshly to him, deal with him only by conciliation."}},{"n":3,"text":"प्रकृत्या पापसत्त्वश्च तुल्यचेताश्च दस्युभिः ।\nऐश्वर्यमदमत्तश्च कृतवैरश्च पाण्डवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By nature he is of sinful mind, with a heart like that of bandits, drunk with the pride of power, and he has made enmity with the Pandavas."}},{"n":4,"text":"अदीर्घदर्शी निष्ठूरी क्षेप्ता क्रूरपराक्रमः ।\nदीर्घमन्युरनेयश्च पापात्मा निकृतिप्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is short-sighted, hard, abusive, cruel in his attacks, holds anger long, cannot be led, is wicked and loves deceit."}},{"n":5,"text":"म्रियेतापि न भज्येत नैव जह्यात्स्वकं मतम् ।\nतादृशेन शमं कृष्ण मन्ये परमदुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He would die rather than bend, and would never give up his own opinion. With such a man, Krishna, I think peace is extremely hard."}},{"n":6,"text":"सुहृदामप्यवाचीनस्त्यक्तधर्मः प्रियानृतः ।\nप्रतिहन्त्येव सुहृदां वाचश्चैव मनांसि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is rude even to friends, has abandoned dharma, loves falsehood, and crushes the words and hearts of his friends."}},{"n":7,"text":"स मन्युवशमापन्नः स्वभावं दुष्टमास्थितः ।\nस्वभावात्पापमन्वेति तृणैस्तुन्न इवोरगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fallen under the sway of anger and fixed in a bad nature, he follows evil by that nature, like a snake goaded with straws."}},{"n":8,"text":"दुर्योधनो हि यत्सेनः सर्वथा विदितस्तव ।\nयच्छीलो यत्स्वभावश्च यद्बलो यत्पराक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You know fully what Duryodhana's army is, his character, his temperament, his strength and his prowess."}},{"n":9,"text":"पुरा प्रसन्नाः कुरवः सहपुत्रास्तथा वयम् ।\nइन्द्रज्येष्ठा इवाभूम मोदमानाः सबान्धवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once the Kurus with their sons, and we also, were happy, like gods with Indra as their eldest, rejoicing with our kinsmen."}},{"n":10,"text":"दुर्योधनस्य क्रोधेन भारता मधुसूदन ।\nधक्ष्यन्ते शिशिरापाये वनानीव हुताशनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, through Duryodhana's anger the Bharatas will be burned, like forests burned by fire when winter ends."}},{"n":11,"text":"अष्टादशेमे राजानः प्रख्याता मधुसूदन ।\nये समुच्चिच्छिदुर्ज्ञातीन्सुहृदश्च सबान्धवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhusudana, there are these eighteen famed kings who destroyed their own kin, friends and relatives."}},{"n":12,"text":"असुराणां समृद्धानां ज्वलतामिव तेजसा ।\nपर्यायकाले धर्मस्य प्राप्ते बलिरजायत ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the turn of dharma came round for the wealthy asuras, blazing with splendor, Bali was born among them."}},{"n":13,"text":"हैहयानामुदावर्तो नीपानां जनमेजयः ।\nबहुलस्तालजङ्घानां कृमीणामुद्धतो वसुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Udavarta among the Haihayas, Janamejaya among the Nipas, Bahula among the Talajanghas, Vasu among the Krimis, born arrogant."}},{"n":14,"text":"अजबिन्दुः सुवीराणां सुराष्ट्राणां कुशर्द्धिकः ।\nअर्कजश्च बलीहानां चीनानां धौतमूलकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ajabindu among the Suviras, Kushardika among the Surashtras, Arkaja among the Balihas, Dhautamulaka among the Chinas."}},{"n":15,"text":"हयग्रीवो विदेहानां वरप्रश्च महौजसाम् ।\nबाहुः सुन्दरवेगानां दीप्ताक्षाणां पुरूरवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hayagriva among the Videhas, Varaprada among the Mahaujas, Bahu among the Sundaravegas, Pururavas among the Diptakshas."}},{"n":16,"text":"सहजश्चेदिमत्स्यानां प्रचेतानां बृहद्बलः ।\nधारणश्चेन्द्रवत्सानां मुकुटानां विगाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sahaja among the Chedis and Matsyas, Brihadbala among the Prachetas, Dharana among the Indravatsas, Vigahana among the Mukutas."}},{"n":17,"text":"शमश्च नन्दिवेगानामित्येते कुलपांसनाः ।\nयुगान्ते कृष्ण संभूताः कुलेषु पुरुषाधमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Shama among the Nandivegas: these were the stains on their families, the lowest of men, born in their clans at the end of an age."}},{"n":18,"text":"अप्ययं नः कुरूणां स्याद्युगान्ते कालसंभृतः ।\nदुर्योधनः कुलाङ्गारो जघन्यः पापपूरुषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So too, Krishna, Duryodhana, the firebrand of his family, base and evil, may be our Kurus' ruin, born with the end of an age."}},{"n":19,"text":"तस्मान्मृदु शनैरेनं ब्रूया धर्मार्थसंहितम् ।\nकामानुबन्धबहुलं नोग्रमुग्रपराक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore speak to him softly and slowly, with words full of dharma and profit and pleasing to his desires; do not be harsh with one whose prowess is harsh."}},{"n":20,"text":"अपि दुर्योधनं कृष्ण सर्वे वयमधश्चराः ।\nनीचैर्भूत्वानुयास्यामो मा स्म नो भरता नशन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, all of us will follow Duryodhana, humbled and bowing low, if only the Bharatas are not destroyed."}},{"n":21,"text":"अप्युदासीनवृत्तिः स्याद्यथा नः कुरुभिः सह ।\nवासुदेव तथा कार्यं न कुरूननयः स्पृशेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva, act so that, even if we keep aloof from the Kurus, no wrong policy touches them."}},{"n":22,"text":"वाच्यः पितामहो वृद्धो ये च कृष्ण सभासदः ।\nभ्रातॄणामस्तु सौभ्रात्रं धार्तराष्ट्रः प्रशाम्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, speak to the old grandsire and to the members of the assembly, so that brotherly feeling may prevail among brothers and the Dhartarashtra be pacified."}},{"n":23,"text":"अहमेतद्ब्रवीम्येवं राजा चैव प्रशंसति ।\nअर्जुनो नैव युद्धार्थी भूयसी हि दयार्जुने ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is what I say, and the king too approves it; Arjuna does not wish for war, for his compassion is the greater."}}]}]}